<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $p: \calJ \rightarrow \Cat _{\infty }^{\lex }$ be a small diagram, which carries each vertex $j \in \calJ $ to an $\infty $-category $\calC _{j}$. Let $\calC $ be a colimit of the diagram $p$ in $\Cat _{\infty }$, and for each $j \in J$, let $\phi _{j}: \calC _{j} \rightarrow \calC $ be the associated functor. Consider the collection of all isomorphism classes of diagrams $\{  f: K^{\triangleleft } \rightarrow \calC \} $, where $K$ is a finite simplicial set and the map $f$ admits a factorization 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  K^{\triangleleft } \stackrel{f_0}{\rightarrow } \calC _{j} \stackrel{\phi _{j}}{\rightarrow } \calC , \]
</div>
    <p>
       where $f_0$ is a limit diagram in $\calC _{j}$. Invoking the dual of Lemma <a href="/tag/7A554B" data-tag="7A554B">6.3.4.2</a>, we deduce the existence of a functor $F: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ with the following properties: 
    <p>
      <ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(1)$"><p>
The $\infty $-category $\calD $ is small and admits finite limits. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(2)$"><p>
Each of the compositions $F \circ \phi _{j}$ is left exact. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(3)$"><p>
For every $\infty $-category $\calE $ which admits finite limits, composition with $F$ induces an equivalence from the full subcategory of $\Fun (\calD , \calE )$ spanned by the left exact functors to the full subcategory of $\Fun ( \calC , \calE )$ spanned by those functors $F': \calC \rightarrow \calE $ such that each $F' \circ \phi _{j}$ is left exact. 
</p>
</li>
</ul>
    <p>
       It follows that that $\calD $ can be identified with a colimit of the diagram $p$ in the $\infty $-category $\Cat _{\infty }^{\lex }$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>